# oodac/ Orphan Symbol Audit

File: openOODA/audit/x86-orphans.oot
Status: orphan-fn scan, 2026-08-25, generated from ooda/oodac/*.oo (top-level fns).

---

```
// # Audit orphan fns in oodac/
//
// Logline: Walk ooda/oodac/*.oo, identify top-level fns with zero external callers, classify them, and rank for deletion.
//
// Setup: openOODA repo at /home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA has 337 .oo files at oodac/; 336 hold top-level fns (1 _template.oo has 0). The repo-wide grep with `\b<name>\b` regex identifies whole-word callers. Fns starting with `_` are private (ignored).
//
// Beats:
//   1. Extract 1724 top-level fn defs from 336 files.
//   2. Classify each fn by caller location: 194 orphan, 388 internal, 1142 external.
//   3. Read each orphan's body and infer a one-line purpose for the audit shortlist.
//   4. Note fns that look orphan but are actually wired (false positive).
```

---

