## 4. False-Positive Notes

Fns that LOOK orphan but are actually wired, or have wired siblings. The audit correctly classifies all of them; this section explains the near-miss cases.

### 4.1 `wui_event_input` / `wui_event_keydown` / `wui_event_resize` / `wui_event_custom` / `wui_patch_type_replace` / `wui_patch_type_update_props` / `wui_patch_type_append_child` / `wui_patch_type_remove_child` (wasm_target_browser.oo)

All 1-line enum-like constants returning 2-5. Their siblings `wui_event_click` and `wui_patch_type_set_text` ARE called from `qa/tests_wasm/test_m4_browser.oo` (external). The 8 orphans are planned siblings of the wired pair; qa tests do not yet exercise them. The audit correctly flags them as orphan.

### 4.2 `mk_ematch`, `mk_ty_cap` in ast.oo (NOT orphan; wired)

Look orphan at first glance. Called from `qa/tests_wasm/test_m2_adversarial.oo`, `test_m2_control.oo`, `test_m3_adt.oo` (mk_ematch) and `qa/tests_wasm/test_m4_caps.oo` (mk_ty_cap). The audit classifies them as external. Their siblings `mk_earrow`, `mk_eclosure`, `mk_resolved` are correctly orphan (planned for Tier 5 #24 typed-AST pipeline).

### 4.3 `c_emit_stream` and `c_emit_stream_toks` (c_emit.oo)

Look like main entry points of the C emit pipeline. Not called from `main.oo` or `cli_emit.oo`; the wired entry is `c_emit_stream_toks_at` (which takes a path argument). The two base fns are older variants that pre-date the path-aware API. Correctly orphan.

### 4.4 `run_emit_llvm_target`, `run_emit_llvm_opt` (cli_emit_llvm.oo)

Look like CLI flag handlers (suffixes for `--target` and `-opt`). Not wired into `main.oo`'s cmd dispatch — `main.oo:245` calls `run_emit_llvm_san` directly. Dead API variants. Correctly orphan.

### 4.5 `gpu_target_metal/spirv/ptx` and `gpu_grid_dim_1d` (gpu_driver.oo)

Look like runtime target constructors. Not called from `cli_gpu_emit.oo:25 run_emit_gpu_cmd`, which dispatches by string match and passes target strings to `gpu_compile_kernel_source` (same file). The struct and constructors are unused. Correctly orphan.

### 4.6 `vm_run_bytecode_caps` (vm_exec.oo, 237 lines)

Looks like a planned VM runner. Imported by `main.oo` (`import "vm_exec.oo"`) but `main.oo:222-227` uses `run_build_san` for `cmd == "run"`. No `cmd == "run-bc"` or `vm` dispatch exists. The fn is a stub entry point for an unwritten CLI command. Correctly orphan.
